{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: the try/catch require silently disables the whole feature with no log**

```js
var sessionDelta = null;
try { sessionDelta = require('./common/sessionDelta.js'); } catch (e) { sessionDelta = null; }
```

Every sibling require in this file is plain; only this one is guarded. If the module ever fails to load (e.g. a pack-omission regression like gh-823), `enrichReworkInputStep`'s `if (sessionDelta && …)` skips the hook **without even a `console.warn`** — session delta silently stops working and nothing in the logs hints why. The gh-823 pin in `test_packRequirePath.js` won't flag this (top-level try is still load-time), but the same incident class is exactly what the silent swallow would hide.

At minimum log the catch (`console.warn('sessionDelta module unavailable (feature disabled):', e)`); better, require it plainly like its siblings — it ships in the same pack closure and `dmtools compile` fails the build on a missing file anyway.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment5.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: `\n---\n` split truncates general-comment bodies containing a horizontal rule**

```js
return section.split(/\n---\n/).map(function(block) {
    return parseSingleMarkdownBlock(block, sourceLabel);
}).filter(Boolean);
```

`buildGeneralCommentsSection` (js/common/githubHelpers.js:380-381) uses `\n---\n` as the *between-comments* delimiter, so a comment body that itself contains a `---` line (horizontal rules are common in GitHub comments, tables, changelogs) is split into extra blocks. The tail blocks don't match the `**author** (date):` pattern and are silently dropped by `.filter(Boolean)` — the snapshot stores, and the resume delta renders, only the body up to the first `---`. Between-leg hashes stay consistent, so the delta doesn't loop, but the model sees a truncated comment.

A body-aware parse (split only on the exact `\n\n---\n\n` separator emitted by the writer) or a richer delimiter in `buildGeneralCommentsSection` would close this.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment7.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: `collectInputFileMap` is blind to subdirectories under `input/<ticket>/`**

```js
listDirSafe(folder, options).forEach(function(entry) {
    var name = String(entry).replace(/^.*\//, '');
    ...
    var content = readFileSafe(folder + '/' + name, options);
```

Entries that are directories yield a `file_read` failure → `null` → skipped, so nested files never enter the snapshot and a changed nested file is forever reported UNCHANGED ("may be trusted from your prior session memory"). Today's writers all produce flat files (`parent-<KEY>.md`, `confluence_output_*.md`, contract files), so this matches the current contract — but the excluded-names check is done on basenames while any future nested layout would silently degrade the delta. Worth either a one-line doc comment stating "flat folder only" or a recursive walk.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment8.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: no dedicated `run_sessionDelta.json` (repo convention)**

Per AGENTS.md ("Add it to the corresponding `run_<module>.json` (or create a new one) and include it in `run_all.json`"), every test module has its own `run_<module>.json` so the suite can be run standalone (`dmtools run js/unit-tests/run_sessionDelta.json`). This PR adds `test_sessionDelta.js` only to `run_all.json:193` — the only way to run it alone today is the full 5.7k-test suite. Every neighboring module (test_forkCheckout, test_configLoader, …) has its own run file; please add one for symmetry.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment9.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: promotion runs twice for the fa provider**

`run_fa` promotes on exit 0 here (fa.sh:135-136) and `run-agent.sh:249-251` promotes again right after `run_fa` returns — same pending file copied twice to the same destination, "📦 Promoted …" logged twice. The run-agent.sh layer is the right single home (it covers all providers); the fa.sh call is redundant — or vice versa, but one layer is enough.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment10.md"}

